Use representative benchmark fixtures and record device/browser/environment metadata. Separate local CPU/GPU work, Worker time and I/O where practical.

## Regression policy
Hot-path changes must compare against current accepted baselines. Large regressions require either a fix or explicit reviewed budget change with user impact explained. Do not game budgets by moving visible work outside the measurement window.

## UX
Longer operations need progress/cancellation only when measurement shows they cross the interaction threshold. Do not add spinners to hide avoidable latency.

## Acceptance
- [ ] Workflow-level performance budget file exists with measurement definitions.
- [ ] Benchmark project covers the protected Core object scale.
- [ ] CI or scheduled evidence catches material regressions on stable environments where feasible.
- [ ] Startup/deferred bundle budgets are enforced.
- [ ] Performance warnings/support diagnostics can identify major bottlenecks without collecting private project content.
- [ ] P1 exit evidence includes measured results rather than qualitative 'feels fast' claims.

Parent: #373
