## Agent working protocol

Before editing:

- fetch the actual current integration authority; never assume `main`;
- read `AGENTS.md`, `.zeus/FAST-KERNEL.md`, the issue, its phase epic and dependencies;
- inspect current open PRs/issues that touch the same files/interfaces;
- follow #317/#319 ownership rules when available; until then, visibly declare the issue/branch/files before editing;
- search for an existing component/system before creating another;
- do not preserve stale planning assumptions when current code differs.

During work, update the child issue at meaningful checkpoints with branch/head SHA, files/interfaces touched, changed assumptions, evidence run, blockers and follow-ups.

Completion requires merged/integrated evidence when the issue contract requires it. A PR opening is not completion.

## Shared-file serialization rule

Different issue numbers do not imply safe parallelism. Root application composition, workspace state, command registry, selection state, design tokens, plan interaction state and canonical persistence bridges must have one active owner or explicit sequencing.

## CTO reconciliation model

Use #369 as the recurring original/CTO-agent lane. After roughly 3-5 merged UI/UX implementation lanes, before every phase gate, or after a cross-cutting contract change, #369 must re-read current repository state, run cross-lane evidence, repair bounded integration drift and refresh this master issue plus the active phase epic.

The CTO reconciler must specifically look for duplicate UI authority, inconsistent selection, undo mismatch, stale responsive states, focus regressions, hidden persistence ambiguity, save/publish wording drift, cross-view divergence, performance cliffs and visual token drift.

## Universal no-go conditions

Do not close any UI/UX child issue if it introduces:

- a second semantic mutation path;
- renderer state as canonical project truth;
- silent data loss or flattening;
- false saved/published/synced wording;
- inaccessible critical controls or keyboard traps;
- colour-only state communication;
- mobile/tablet regressions hidden by desktop screenshots;
- a local token/component duplicate where an existing system should be extended;
- unexplained disabled controls or destructive errors without recovery where recovery is possible;
- visual baseline updates that merely hide a regression;
- unmeasured hot-path performance regressions.

## Master exit condition

Close only when UX-0 through UX-8 have passed their exit gates or an explicit owner-approved plan revision supersedes this programme and records what remains and why.

