## Role

This issue defines the recurring **original/CTO agent** the programme needs after parallel implementation agents have completed work.

The CTO reconciler does not compete with active feature owners. It periodically gathers merged/completed lanes, verifies that the repository still behaves as one product, repairs integration defects, updates the capability/programme state, and opens bounded follow-up issues when needed.

## Trigger cadence

Run a reconciliation pass when any of these is true:

- 3 to 5 programme implementation PRs have merged since the last pass;
- a phase gate is about to be evaluated;
- a persistence, semantic-model, renderer, file-format, Agent or connector contract changed;
- a cross-lane regression is reported;
- the master programme snapshot is more than 7 days stale during active development;
- the owner explicitly requests a reconciliation pass.

Do not run continuous churn after every trivial merge.

## Required reconciliation pass

1. Fetch the actual current integration authority. Never assume the branch name.
2. Read all programme issues/PRs merged since the previous checkpoint.
3. Inspect unresolved review comments and known follow-ups.
4. Rebuild the current capability graph/ledger from repository evidence.
5. Run the broad exact-head evidence set required by the changed surfaces.
6. Test the protected user workflow as far as currently reachable.
7. Look specifically for integration classes that individual lanes often miss:
   - duplicate authority;
   - semantic flattening;
   - stale derived state;
   - wrong project/document identity;
   - undo/redo mismatch;
   - save/publish/sync wording drift;
   - import/export fidelity drift;
   - focus/keyboard/touch regressions;
   - performance cliffs;
   - stale claims/evidence;
   - incompatible migrations;
   - Agent/connector permission drift;
   - dead code or library-without-caller regressions.
8. Fix bounded integration defects that are safely within the reconciliation scope.
9. For non-bounded or disputed changes, open a dedicated issue instead of silently broadening scope.
10. Update #367 and the active phase epic with current verified state, blockers and the next safe work frontier.

## CTO repair authority

The reconciler may fix cross-lane integration defects only when the intended behaviour is already clear from stronger sources of truth. It must not use this issue to invent product scope, decide unresolved architecture choices, override ADRs, or merge around human/legal/research gates.

## Required output after each pass

Post one structured checkpoint comment containing:

- integration branch + exact head SHA;
- merged programme issues/PRs included;
- evidence run and results;
- regressions found;
- repairs made;
- new bounded follow-up issues opened;
- remaining blockers;
- phase-gate status;
- updated Core 1.0 and current-phase maturity based on verified capabilities, not issue count;
- recommended next safe parallel lanes.

## Reconciliation evidence

At minimum, choose evidence based on affected surfaces and include:

- format/lint/type/build;
- relevant unit/property tests;
- native `.arq` open/save/publish/reopen checks when project state changed;
- real-browser capability checks for user-reachable changes;
