- #360 Firefox support envelope
- #364 active work board

Current open PRs must be treated as legacy ownership until the ZEUS claim protocol is enforced. At programme creation time these include #361, #362, #363, #365 and research-only #366.

## Programme completion model

Do not report one global percentage from issue count. Track separately:

- **Core 1.0 maturity**
- **current phase gate completion**
- **mature-programme maturity**
- **human/external evidence debt**

The authoritative state should eventually come from a generated capability ledger, not hand-maintained prose.

## Phase-gate rule

Atomic implementation issues may be created ahead of time only when their contracts and dependencies are already stable. Later phases must remain gated epics until the previous phase has passed its exit gate and the repository has been re-read. This prevents future agents from implementing stale assumptions.

## Universal issue contract

Every implementation issue in this programme must state:

- user outcome;
- current evidence / known gap;
- in-scope and out-of-scope work;
- dependencies and likely ownership conflicts;
- canonical data/operation implications;
- UI/UX states including loading, empty, success, failure, disabled and recovery states where relevant;
- persistence/recovery implications;
- security/privacy implications;
- accessibility and input implications;
- performance implications;
- required tests and exact-head evidence;
- acceptance criteria;
- handoff notes for the ZEUS reconciler.

## Universal no-go conditions

No programme issue may be declared complete if it knowingly introduces any of these:

- silent semantic loss or flattening;
- a second canonical persistence/publication authority;
- false saved/synced/published wording;
- wrong-document or stale-document connector writes;
- AI mutation bypassing deterministic validation/approval rules;
- silent unit/coordinate conversion;
- renderer/cache state becoming canonical project data;
- unverified physical-device claims from simulation only;
- hidden import/export loss;
- data-loss recovery paths that exist only in unit tests and not through the product path;
- inaccessible critical interaction or keyboard trap;
- a merge that conflicts with another active lane without reconciliation.

## Master exit condition

This issue closes only when P10 has passed its gate or when an explicit owner-approved programme revision supersedes this trajectory and records what remains, what changed, and why.

## Agent working rule

Agents should work from bounded child issues, not directly from this master issue. This issue is programme authority and progress aggregation only. After each merged lane, the designated ZEUS CTO reconciler updates programme state, integration debt and the next safe work frontier.

